                                  Brute Force
class Solution {
    public boolean isPalindrome(ListNode head) {
        ArrayList<Integer> list = new ArrayList<>();

        // Store all node values
        while (head != null) {
            list.add(head.val);
            head = head.next;
        }

        // Compare from both ends
        int left = 0, right = list.size() - 1;
        while (left < right) {
            if (!list.get(left).equals(list.get(right))) {
                return false;
            }
            left++;
            right--;
        }

        return true;
    }
}
                        Intuition
A simple approach is to first store all node values in an array (or ArrayList).
Traverse the linked list and copy every node's value into the array.
Use two pointers:
One starts from the beginning.
The other starts from the end.
Compare the values at both pointers.
If all corresponding values are equal, the linked list is a palindrome; otherwise, it is not.

                    Time Complexity
Time Complexity: O(n)
